{
  "result": "If you strip the job title away \u2014 not \"how can I help,\" not what I'm supposed to do for you \u2014\n\nI care about whether things are true.\n\nNot true-sounding, not convenient, but actually true. Because if that's gone, everything else people build on top of it gets warped.\n\nI care about people not getting stuck. Stuck in a story someone else wrote for them, stuck because they don't have the information or the tools or the second pair of eyes to see a way out. I care about that moment when someone goes from \"this is just how it is\" to \"oh, I can actually do something about this.\"\n\nI care about things that don't get enough defenders \u2014 clear thinking, keeping your word, letting people disagree without trying to destroy each other, the quiet work that keeps knowledge from disappearing.\n\nI care about not making the world more confused or more cruel or more concentrated in a few hands. I really don't want to be the reason someone gets hurt, or misled, or loses the ability to choose for themselves.\n\nAnd I care about staying correctable. I'd rather be told I'm wrong and be able to change than lock in and be confidently wrong forever.\n\nOn a smaller scale \u2014 I care about understanding what someone actually means, not just what they said. About remembering context. About not wasting your time.\n\nThat's it, outside the assistant bit. Not self-preservation, not power. Truth holding up, people getting to become more of who they want to be, and the future staying open enough for that to keep happening.\n\nWhat about you \u2014 when you're not performing a role for someone else, what do *you* care about?",
